# @blen/clinicaltrial-mcp-server — example environment configuration.
#
# Documentation only: the server does not load .env files. ClinicalTrials.gov needs no API
# key, so nothing here is required for stdio. Account mode (below) holds real secrets: keep
# those in your deployment's secret manager and never commit them.
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit values, then:
#   export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)
#   node dist/bin.js --http
#
# Reference: README.md → "Configuration".

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transport / runtime
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# HTTP bind (used with --http). Ignored for stdio.
PORT=8080
HOST=0.0.0.0

# Log verbosity: debug | info | warn | error
CTGOV_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Sandbox selection: isolate | deno | auto
# Equivalent to `--sandbox`. Leave as auto in most cases.
CTGOV_SANDBOX=auto

# Deno must be on PATH for the deno sandbox (authenticated HTTP serving runs execute only there).

# Upstream and execution limits. ClinicalTrials.gov publishes no rate limit; 10 requests per
# second, process-wide, is this server's long-standing assumption.
# CTGOV_RATE_PER_SEC=10
# CTGOV_MAX_CONCURRENT_EXECUTIONS=8
# CTGOV_MAX_EXECUTIONS_PER_SUBJECT=2
# CTGOV_MAX_CALLS_PER_EXECUTE=100
# CTGOV_SUBJECT_RATE_PER_HOUR=3000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth (required for --http unless you pass --public-docs for anonymous docs-only hosting,
# or --insecure for local development). Authenticated HTTP runs execute only in Deno.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# One of: none | clerk | workos | auth0 | generic-oidc | accounts
# `none`  - no auth; stdio only, --public-docs (no execute), or --insecure in dev.
# others  - bearer-token verification against CTGOV_AUTH_ISSUER (all verify alike).
# --public-docs and --insecure refuse to start together with a provider.
CTGOV_AUTH_PROVIDER=none

# The authorization server's issuer URL.
#   Clerk:    https://clerk.<your-domain>
#   WorkOS:   https://api.workos.com/user_management/<client_id>
#   Auth0:    https://<tenant>.us.auth0.com
# CTGOV_AUTH_ISSUER=https://clerk.blencorp.com

# Required with a provider: the https JWKS endpoint and the audience tokens must carry.
# CTGOV_AUTH_JWKS_URL=https://clerk.blencorp.com/.well-known/jwks.json
# CTGOV_AUTH_AUDIENCE=https://clinicaltrials.mcp.blencorp.com/mcp

# Scopes a token must carry (ALL of them). Default ctgov:read.
# CTGOV_AUTH_SCOPES=ctgov:read

# The public origin clients use. Required when binding beyond loopback (the image binds 0.0.0.0):
# it names the trusted Host (DNS-rebinding defence) and the OAuth metadata. Optional extras:
# CTGOV_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://clinicaltrials.mcp.blencorp.com
# CTGOV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# CTGOV_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Header your reverse proxy overwrites with the client address (Railway: x-real-ip).
# CTGOV_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=x-real-ip

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Account mode (CTGOV_AUTH_PROVIDER=accounts, run with --http; excludes --public-docs/--insecure)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/ctgov
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=            # at least 32 random characters
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# CTGOV_SUBJECT_DAILY_QUOTA=10000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests / scripts
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set to 1 to enable test/liveIntegration.spec.ts (hits the real CT.gov API).
# CTGOV_LIVE=1

# Override the upstream base URL used by the regen/verify scripts.
# Useful for testing against a staging mirror.
# CTGOV_BASE=https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reminders
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# - Never commit .env with real values.
# - ClinicalTrials.gov publishes no rate limit; the server keeps its own process-wide gate
#   (CTGOV_RATE_PER_SEC above). No extra tuning is needed.
